<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Edgars yr shr dips, div steady.</title>
<headline>Edgars yr shr dips, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  598.0	 vs 642.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 247.0	 vs 247.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   320.9	 vs 337.2</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters expected earnings at a consensus 638 cents per share, while the final dividend was expected flat at 247 cents.</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   495.5	 vs 506.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 170.5	 vs 180.8</p>
<p>    Financing costs	 51.8	  vs 72.9</p>
<p>    Turnover		  5,888.1     vs 5,325.8</p>
<p>Full name: Edgars Stores Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said capitalisation shares will be awarded to shareholders registered on May 30. The number of shares to which shareholders will be entitled will be determined by the ratio that 180 cents multiplied by 1.06 bears to the weighted average closing price of the firm's shares on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange for the four days ending June 26.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
